content.thinking:
The failure: "产品当前无已生效备案" for round 1 (P-CX-1, P-CD-1, etc.) — round 0 works, round 1 fails. Why? Because in the loop, round 0's `makeAdultEffective` sets clock to EXPIRY and expires notices. Round 1: `makeAdultEffective("REQ-CF-1", "P-CD-1")` submits at clock=EXPIRY (2026-07-10T00:00:00Z) — the submit time is now EXPIRY, so the new filing's public notice expires at EXPIRY+10 days = 2026-07-20. Then `clock.setInstant(EXPIRY)` (same time) and `expireDuePublicNotices` — the new filing's expiresAt is 2026-07-20 > EXPIRY, so it's not due → not effective → register fails.

Fix: in makeAdultEffective, advance clock beyond the new expiry. Better: set clock to a time after submit + 10 days. Since clock is already at EXPIRY from previous round, submitting at EXPIRY gives expiry 2026-07-20. So in the helper, after submit, advance clock by 11 days from current: `clock.setInstant(clock.instant().plus(11, ChronoUnit.DAYS))` then expire. Let me make the helper robust:

```java
private void makeAdultEffective(String reqId, String product) {
    filingService.submit(FilingFixtures.ordinarySubmit(reqId, product));
    clock.setInstant(clock.instant().plus(11, ChronoUnit.DAYS));
    filingService.expireDuePublicNotices(null);
}
```

Same for the lifecycle test helpers (makeAdultEffective/makeChildEffective use fixed EXPIRY — same issue across tests? No — each test method gets fresh clock reset to INITIAL_NOW by @BeforeEach. Within a single test method, makeAdultEffective is called twice in drawRejectsCrossProductBatch (P-LP-9A and P-LP-9B) — that's why it failed too! First call: submit at INITIAL_NOW, set EXPIRY, expire → effective. Second call: submit at EXPIRY → expires 2026-07-20; set EXPIRY again → not due → fails.

Fix with the +11 days approach in both test classes. Also substantiveChangeEffectuationDisablesOldPrintRun uses NEXT_EXPIRY = 2026-07-20 — the substantive change submitted at EXPIRY (2026-07-10) gets notice date 2026-07-10, expires 2026-07-20 → NEXT_EXPIRY works. Good.

Let me update both helpers.

